// `namespace` is retired surface syntax. A module's path is derived from where its file sits, so a
// declaration is redundant by construction and cannot disagree without one of the two being wrong —
// the parser refuses it and says so, rather than leaving a reader of older code with an unexpected
// token. The node itself lives on internally: the loader writes each derived path into the program
// under it.
// expect: error E0072 at 1:1
// expect: exit 1
use lib.thing.f;

echo f()
